# What I Learned

# 1. Coordinate mapping

For matrix rotation, instead of thinking about swapping values randomly, identify:

text
old position → new position


For clockwise rotation:

python
(i, j) → (n - 1 - j, i)


# 2. Python 2D list creation

Avoid:

python
[[-1] * n] * n


Use:

python
[[-1] * n for _ in range(n)]


# 3. Index vs size

If matrix size is:

text
n = 3


last index is:

text
n - 1 = 2


This is why rotation formulas commonly contain:

python
n - 1


# 4. Extra space

My current solution uses `O(n²)` extra space.

A better interview solution can rotate the matrix **in-place** using `O(1)` extra space by:

text
Transpose
+
Reverse each row


That is the next optimization to learn.

